IMPORT prelude

-- Wyoming POWER (Personal Opportunities With Employment Responsibilities), the state's TANF cash assistance, and the state SSI
-- supplement and burial assistance: Wyoming Statutes Title 42 chapter 2 (the Public Assistance and Social Services Act), with
-- the Department of Family Services' POWER rule (049.0030 Chapter 1) brought in -- what a family meets: the dependent child
-- (W.S. 42-2-104(b)), the asset test (rule s 6(a)(x), W.S. 42-2-109(b)), the earned income disregard (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(iv);
-- rule s 9(a)(v)), the maximum payment test and the performance payment (rule s 9(a)(vii)(B)), the earned income incentive (rule
-- s 9(a)(vii)(B)(X)), the five-year limit and its exemptions (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(i)), veterans' disability compensation not counted
-- (W.S. 42-2-106(c)), the duty to report a change within ten days (W.S. 42-2-109(b); rule s 9(a)(vii)(G)), burial assistance
-- (W.S. 42-2-103(c)) and the state SSI supplement (W.S. 42-2-103(d)).
--
-- SEAT: the caretaker relative applying for or receiving POWER for a dependent child ("Is my child a dependent child? Are we
-- under the asset limit? What is our payment? Do the five years apply to us? What must I report, and by when?"), and the SSI
-- recipient asking about the state supplement.
--
-- Edition: the Legislative Service Office's title 42 PDF (created 2026-05-08), downloaded 2026-10-19, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/wy-stat-42-ch02.txt; and the POWER rule, Chapter 1 (Reference 049.0030.1.01122018, in effect
-- from 01/12/2018), from rules.wyo.gov, deposited in the sibling subject
-- ../../../wyoming-administrative-rules-049-0030-chapter-1-power-program/registers/source-bundle/wy-rules-049-0030-ch1-power.txt.
--
-- AMOUNTS. W.S. 42-2-103(e)(iii) prints the 2008 maximum POWER payment table and adjusts it each July from 2009 by the Wyoming
-- cost-of-living index; the current figures are not published as a rule and are not deposited. The maximum payment for the
-- family is therefore an INPUT (with the 2008 table kept as `the 2008 maximum POWER payment`). The shelter qualified or
-- disqualified distinction (rule s 9(a)(iv)) is folded into that input. The state SSI supplement amount is set in the budget:
-- not computed.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Medicaid (art. 4); child care copayments (W.S. 42-2-103(f)); the individual earned income disregard of
-- 42-2-103(e)(iv)(A)-(G) (discretionary, not reviewable); deeming of stepparent, minor parent's parents and sponsor income (rule
-- s 9(a)(vi)); Pay-After-Performance work and child support requirements (rule ss 7, 8) except as the reporting duty; the
-- domestic violence waivers (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(viii)) except as a fact for the time limit; minor parents (42-2-103(e)(ii)).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wyoming POWER and public assistance -- W.S. 42-2-101 to 42-2-115, with DFS rule 049.0030 ch. 1`

§§ `The parties and the actions`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `the department`

DECLARE `Action` IS ONE OF
    `notify the department of the change`
    `provide the verifications requested`

§§ `W.S. 42-2-104(b) -- the dependent child`

-- 42-2-104(b): "a dependent child includes any child who is under eighteen (18) years of age and living with a relative in a
-- residence maintained by the relative as determined by rule and regulation of the department, regularly attending school or its
-- equivalent as determined by the department, or is expected to graduate from high school before the age of nineteen (19) years.
-- For purposes of this subsection, a dependent child does not include a minor parent." Rule s 9(a)(ii)(B): "up to age 18 or up
-- to age 19 when expected to graduate from high school prior to attaining age 19". Read as: living with a relative, and either
-- under 18 or, if 18, expected to graduate before 19; school attendance as the department determines is asked (NOTES.md finding 1).
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `lives with a relative in a home the relative maintains` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regularly attends school or its equivalent, or is not of school age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `expected to graduate from high school before 19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a minor parent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dependent child for POWER` IF
        `lives with a relative in a home the relative maintains`
    AND (NOT (`is a minor parent`))
    AND (   (`age` LESS THAN 18 AND `regularly attends school or its equivalent, or is not of school age`)
         OR (`age` LESS THAN 19 AND `expected to graduate from high school before 19`))

§§ `Rule s 6(a)(x), W.S. 42-2-109(b) -- assets`

-- Rule s 6(a)(x)(A): "All the combined assets of the assistance unit will not exceed the limit of $5,000, excluding the vehicles
-- exempted under (E)." W.S. 42-2-109(b): "The department shall exempt not more than two (2) licensed motor vehicles from personal
-- assets". (The other exempt assets of the rule's Appendix A are left out of the figure the person states.)
GIVEN `countable assets other than up to two licensed vehicles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the POWER asset limit` IF
    `countable assets other than up to two licensed vehicles` AT MOST 5000

§§ `W.S. 42-2-103(e)(iii)-(iv), 42-2-106(c); rule s 9 -- the payment`

-- W.S. 42-2-103(e)(iii): the maximum POWER payment "for the year 2008", by family size: 1 $290, 2 $476, 3 $506, 4 $506, 5 $536,
-- 6 $536, 7 and above $566 ("Cumulative Inflation Factor 1.489"), adjusted each July from 2009 by the Wyoming cost-of-living index.
GIVEN `family size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2008 maximum POWER payment` `family size` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `family size` AT MOST 1 THEN 290
        IF `family size` EQUALS 2 THEN 476
        IF `family size` AT MOST 4 THEN 506
        IF `family size` AT MOST 6 THEN 536
        OTHERWISE 566

-- W.S. 42-2-103(e)(iv): "only one (1) earned income disregard ... at six hundred dollars ($600.00) per month for any one (1)
-- recipient. For married couples the earned income disregard shall be one thousand two hundred dollars ($1,200.00) per month."
-- Rule s 9(a)(v)(B): the $1,200 is for "an eligible married couple ... with a child in common regardless of whether both are
-- employed".
GIVEN `a married couple with a child in common` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earned income disregard` `a married couple with a child in common` MEANS
    IF `a married couple with a child in common` THEN 1200 ELSE 600

-- W.S. 42-2-106(c): "compensation received for a veteran's service connected disability shall not be counted in determining
-- income if that compensation on an annual basis is not more than the poverty level for the applicant".
GIVEN `monthly veterans' disability compensation` IS A NUMBER
      `annual poverty level for the applicant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the veterans' compensation counted` `monthly veterans' disability compensation` `annual poverty level for the applicant` MEANS
    IF (`monthly veterans' disability compensation` TIMES 12) AT MOST `annual poverty level for the applicant`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `monthly veterans' disability compensation`

-- Rule s 9(a)(vii)(B), the maximum payment test: "(I) The anticipated gross earned income of the assistance unit, excluding the
-- earned income of a dependent child who is a full-time high school student under the age of 18 ... (II) The $600 or $1200
-- earned income disregard is deducted. (III) The anticipated unearned income is added including: (1.) Child or spousal support
-- ... (V) The balance is compared against the maximum payment for the number of eligible individuals. (VI) The case shall be
-- eligible when the balance in (V) is less than the maximum payment. (VII) The performance payment shall be calculated by
-- subtracting the balance in (V)." Earned income below the disregard counts as nil.
DECLARE `Payment outcome` IS ONE OF
    `not eligible: the balance is not less than the maximum payment (rule s 9(a)(vii)(B)(VI))`
    `a performance payment of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `maximum payment` IS A NUMBER
      `monthly gross earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `disregard` IS A NUMBER
      `monthly unearned income counted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Payment outcome`
`the performance payment` `maximum payment` `monthly gross earned income` `disregard` `monthly unearned income counted` MEANS
    IF `balance` LESS THAN `maximum payment`
    THEN `a performance payment of` (`maximum payment` MINUS `balance`)
    ELSE `not eligible: the balance is not less than the maximum payment (rule s 9(a)(vii)(B)(VI))`
    WHERE
        `balance` MEANS (max 0 (`monthly gross earned income` MINUS `disregard`)) PLUS `monthly unearned income counted`

-- Rule s 9(a)(vii)(B)(X): "The earned income incentive shall be available for up to six (6) consecutive months after the
-- assistance unit has become ineligible for a regular performance payment because of earned income"; "c. The amount ... is based
-- on 50% of the maximum payment level for the assistance unit size as long as the family member remains employed".
GIVEN `maximum payment` IS A NUMBER
      `ineligible because of earned income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months of incentive already counted` IS A NUMBER
      `still employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earned income incentive` `maximum payment` `ineligible because of earned income` `months of incentive already counted` `still employed` MEANS
    IF `ineligible because of earned income` AND `still employed` AND `months of incentive already counted` LESS THAN 6
    THEN `maximum payment` TIMES 50%
    ELSE 0

§§ `W.S. 42-2-103(e)(i) -- the five years`

DECLARE `Time limit outcome` IS ONE OF
    `within the five-year lifetime limit`
    `not subject to the limit: totally disabled, or the full-time carer of a totally disabled or incapacitated family member (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(i))`
    `past five years, but an extension applies (abandonment, or continuing an associate or baccalaureate degree in the state-funded program)`
    `past five years, but the time limit is waived for domestic violence (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(viii))`
    `past the five-year lifetime limit`

-- W.S. 42-2-103(e)(i): assistance is limited "to five (5) years for any assistance unit within a lifetime, regardless of
-- location", federal and state months added together. "Any individual who is totally physically or mentally disabled ... or who
-- is a caretaker and stays at home to provide full-time care for a totally disabled or incapacitated immediate family member ...
-- shall not be subject to the limitation". Extensions are listed for "(B) Continuation of education leading toward an associate
-- or a baccalaureate degree under the state funded program only; (C) Abandonment." (e)(viii): the department may waive program
-- requirements for victims of domestic violence, "other than time limits which shall be waived under paragraph (i)" (asked as a
-- fact). Months as a dependent child do not count against an adult's own unit (except one year for a minor parent; the person
-- states the months that count).
GIVEN `months of assistance counted` IS A NUMBER
      `totally disabled, or full-time carer of a totally disabled family member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an extension for abandonment or degree completion applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time limit is waived for domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Time limit outcome`
`the five-year limit` `months of assistance counted` `totally disabled, or full-time carer of a totally disabled family member` `an extension for abandonment or degree completion applies` `the time limit is waived for domestic violence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `totally disabled, or full-time carer of a totally disabled family member`
        THEN `not subject to the limit: totally disabled, or the full-time carer of a totally disabled or incapacitated family member (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(i))`
        IF `months of assistance counted` LESS THAN 60
        THEN `within the five-year lifetime limit`
        IF `an extension for abandonment or degree completion applies`
        THEN `past five years, but an extension applies (abandonment, or continuing an associate or baccalaureate degree in the state-funded program)`
        IF `the time limit is waived for domestic violence`
        THEN `past five years, but the time limit is waived for domestic violence (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(viii))`
        OTHERWISE `past the five-year lifetime limit`

§§ `W.S. 42-2-109(b); rule s 9(a)(vii)(G) -- reporting changes`

-- W.S. 42-2-109(b): "Upon gaining possession of any property, income or other assets after receiving any public assistance ... a
-- recipient shall notify the department not later than ten (10) calendar days after becoming aware of the change". Rule s
-- 9(a)(vii)(G): "A change in circumstances shall be reported not later than 10 calendar days after the change becomes known ...
-- The applicant/recipient shall provide verifications needed ... not later than 10 days from the date of a notice requesting the
-- verification." Rule s 9(b)(xii)(C): "an unreported or untimely reported adverse change shall be considered noncompliance and
-- the noncompliance penalty shall be applied." Counted in days from becoming aware (or from the notice).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my duty to report a change` MEANS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    MUST   `notify the department of the change`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the recipient` BECAUSE "change not reported within 10 calendar days: the noncompliance penalty applies (W.S. 42-2-109(b); rule s 9(b)(xii)(C))"

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my duty to provide verifications` MEANS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    MUST   `provide the verifications requested`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the recipient` BECAUSE "verifications not provided within 10 days of the notice (rule s 9(a)(vii)(G))"

§§ `W.S. 42-2-103(c)-(d) -- burial assistance and the state SSI supplement`

-- 42-2-103(c): burial or cremation expenses of a recipient of POWER, SSI or Medicaid at death "without sufficient means in his own
-- estate or other resources": "The amount paid ... shall not exceed one thousand five hundred dollars ($1,500.00) after
-- consideration of funds available ... from all other sources", plus up to $500 for transport to the veteran's cemetery for a
-- qualifying veteran; cemetery costs excluded.
GIVEN `burial or cremation expenses, excluding cemetery costs` IS A NUMBER
      `funds available from all other sources` IS A NUMBER
      `a veteran qualifying for burial at the veteran's cemetery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `transport to the veteran's cemetery` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the burial assistance` `burial or cremation expenses, excluding cemetery costs` `funds available from all other sources` `a veteran qualifying for burial at the veteran's cemetery` `transport to the veteran's cemetery` MEANS
    (min 1500 (max 0 (`burial or cremation expenses, excluding cemetery costs` MINUS `funds available from all other sources`))) PLUS `transport`
    WHERE
        `transport` MEANS IF `a veteran qualifying for burial at the veteran's cemetery` THEN min 500 `transport to the veteran's cemetery` ELSE 0

-- 42-2-103(d): the department of health's program "entitling any individual receiving payments under the federal supplemental
-- security income program with no other income during any one (1) calendar month, to a payment for each month the condition
-- exists." The amount is set in the budget.
GIVEN `I receive federal SSI this month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have any other income this month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to the state SSI supplement` IF
    `I receive federal SSI this month` AND NOT (`I have any other income this month`)

§ `Questions for the applicant`

§§ `Is my child eligible, and are we under the asset limit?`

@export Is my child a "dependent child" for Wyoming POWER (W.S. 42-2-104(b))?
GIVEN `my child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in whole years
      `my child lives with a relative in that relative's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child lives with a relative in a residence the relative maintains
      `my child attends school regularly, or is not of school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child regularly attends school or its equivalent (answer yes for a child too young for school)
      `my child is expected to graduate from high school before 19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an 18-year-old: whether the child is expected to graduate from high school before turning 19
      `my child is a minor parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a minor who is a parent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my child a dependent child for POWER` IF
    `is a dependent child for POWER` `my child's age` `my child lives with a relative in that relative's home` `my child attends school regularly, or is not of school age` `my child is expected to graduate from high school before 19` `my child is a minor parent`

@export Are we under the POWER asset limit of $5,000 (DFS rule 049.0030 ch. 1 s 6(a)(x); W.S. 42-2-109(b))?
GIVEN `our countable assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The combined countable assets of the assistance unit in US dollars, leaving out up to two licensed motor vehicles and the other assets the rule exempts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are we under the POWER asset limit` IF
    `meets the POWER asset limit` `our countable assets`

§§ `What is our payment?`

@export What was the 2008 maximum POWER payment for our family size (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(iii))? It has been adjusted every July since 2009.
GIVEN `our family size` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of eligible people in the assistance unit
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What was the 2008 maximum POWER payment` `our family size` MEANS
    `the 2008 maximum POWER payment` `our family size`

@export What is our monthly POWER performance payment (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(iv), 42-2-106(c); DFS rule s 9(a)(vii)(B))?
GIVEN `our maximum payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The current maximum POWER payment for your family size (shelter qualified or disqualified), in US dollars: the 2008 table adjusted each year by the Wyoming cost-of-living index
      `our monthly gross earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The assistance unit's anticipated monthly gross earnings, in US dollars, leaving out a full-time high school student under 18's earnings
      `we are a married couple with a child in common` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible married couple applying with a child in common (the disregard is $1,200 instead of $600)
      `our monthly child or spousal support and other unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Anticipated monthly unearned income, in US dollars, including child or spousal support, but not veterans' disability compensation
      `monthly veterans' disability compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc Monthly compensation for a veteran's service-connected disability, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `the annual poverty level for us` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal poverty level for the applicant for a year, in US dollars
GIVETH A `Payment outcome`
`What is our POWER payment` `our maximum payment` `our monthly gross earned income` `we are a married couple with a child in common` `our monthly child or spousal support and other unearned income` `monthly veterans' disability compensation` `the annual poverty level for us` MEANS
    `the performance payment` `our maximum payment` `our monthly gross earned income` (`the earned income disregard` `we are a married couple with a child in common`) (`our monthly child or spousal support and other unearned income` PLUS `the veterans' compensation counted` `monthly veterans' disability compensation` `the annual poverty level for us`)

@export How much is our POWER earned income incentive after earnings end our regular payment (DFS rule s 9(a)(vii)(B)(X))?
GIVEN `our maximum payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum POWER payment for your assistance unit size, in US dollars
      `earnings made us ineligible for a regular payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the family became ineligible for a regular performance payment because of earned income
      `incentive months already counted` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the six consecutive incentive months have already passed
      `the family member is still employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the family member remains employed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is our earned income incentive` `our maximum payment` `earnings made us ineligible for a regular payment` `incentive months already counted` `the family member is still employed` MEANS
    `the earned income incentive` `our maximum payment` `earnings made us ineligible for a regular payment` `incentive months already counted` `the family member is still employed`

§§ `Do the five years apply to us?`

@export Can our assistance unit still receive POWER under the five-year lifetime limit (W.S. 42-2-103(e)(i), (viii))?
GIVEN `months of assistance that count` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of POWER, AFDC or TANF (federal or state-funded, in any state) count against your assistance unit; months you received as a dependent child do not count, except one year as a minor parent
      `I am totally disabled, or the full-time carer of a totally disabled family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are totally physically or mentally disabled, or stay at home to give full-time care to a totally disabled or incapacitated immediate family member living with you because no other reasonable care is available
      `an extension for abandonment or degree completion applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department has extended the limit for abandonment or desertion, or to continue an associate or baccalaureate degree in the state-funded program
      `the limit is waived for domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time limit is waived because you are fleeing for your or your children's safety or have been, or are at risk of being, a victim of domestic violence
GIVETH A `Time limit outcome`
`Can we still receive POWER under the five-year limit` `months of assistance that count` `I am totally disabled, or the full-time carer of a totally disabled family member` `an extension for abandonment or degree completion applies` `the limit is waived for domestic violence` MEANS
    `the five-year limit` `months of assistance that count` `I am totally disabled, or the full-time carer of a totally disabled family member` `an extension for abandonment or degree completion applies` `the limit is waived for domestic violence`

§§ `SSI recipients, and burial`

-- Situation: only for a person on federal SSI, or for the family of a recipient who has died.

@export Am I entitled to Wyoming's state SSI supplement this month (W.S. 42-2-103(d))?
GIVEN `I receive federal SSI this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive federal Supplemental Security Income payments this calendar month
      `I have any other income this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have any income other than SSI this calendar month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to the state SSI supplement` IF
    `is entitled to the state SSI supplement` `I receive federal SSI this month` `I have any other income this month`

@export How much will the state pay towards the burial of a POWER, SSI or Medicaid recipient (W.S. 42-2-103(c))?
GIVEN `burial or cremation expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The burial or cremation expenses, not counting cemetery costs, in US dollars
      `funds available from all other sources` IS A NUMBER @desc Money available from the person's estate and all other sources for the burial, in US dollars
      `the person was a veteran qualifying for the veteran's cemetery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person was a veteran who qualifies for burial at the veteran's cemetery
      `transport to the veteran's cemetery` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost of transport to the veteran's cemetery, in US dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much burial assistance` `burial or cremation expenses` `funds available from all other sources` `the person was a veteran qualifying for the veteran's cemetery` `transport to the veteran's cemetery` MEANS
    `the burial assistance` `burial or cremation expenses` `funds available from all other sources` `the person was a veteran qualifying for the veteran's cemetery` `transport to the veteran's cemetery`
